OL,3,ABangkok roads submerged as flood
OL,4,Adisaster declared
OL,5,
OL,6,FA flood emergency disaster has been
OL,7,Fdeclared across Bangkok after more than
OL,8,F300mm (12in) of rain fell since
OL,9,FThursday, leaving roads in the Thai
OL,10,Fcapital submerged.
OL,12,FOn Sunday, Bangkok's Metropolitan
OL,13,FAuthority said the rains have subsided,
OL,14,Fbut canal water levels remain high. The
OL,15,Fcity's governor has warned that the
OL,16,Fflooding is not yet over.
OL,18,FPeople have been urged to stay at home
OL,19,Fand those living close to the city's
OL,20,Fnetwork of canals have been advised to
OL,21,Fmove their belongings to upper floors.
OL,23,APub: 26-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
